<title>SINGAPORE: TABLE-Keppel Finance 1H net up 7.0 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Keppel Finance 1H net up 7.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30, 1997</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			 13.75  vs  12.87</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)		 6.51  vs   6.34</p>
<p>    Operating income		 41.26  vs  39.63</p>
<p>    Other income			0.44  vs   0.80</p>
<p>    Total income		     41.70  vs  40.44</p>
<p>    Operating profit		 19.98  vs  18.53</p>
<p>    Interest expense		  1.01  vs   0.70</p>
<p>    Pretax			     18.71  vs  17.55</p>
<p>    TAx				   4.96  vs   4.68</p>
<p>Note - Keppel Finance Ltd, a unit of Keppel Corp, said the local property and car markets were not expected to make a quick turnaround in the second half.</p>
